@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Worker Contact Role API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Account API Permissioning functionality in relation to Worker Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Worker Role" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Worker Role  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Assign contact role to worker contact attempt
	Koroneiki worker contacts should not be able to be assigned to account contact roles on accounts by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Region       | United States                            |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I attempt to assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a non permissioned user	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

Scenario: Assign contact role to worker contact attempt via uuid attempt
	Koroneiki worker contacts should not be able to be assigned to account contact roles on accounts via contact uuid by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Region       | United States                            |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I attempt to assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles via uuid as a non permissioned user	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Member" visible via uuid to a non permissioned user

Scenario: View contact role from worker contact attempt
	Koroneiki worker account contact roles assigned to contacts should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region       | United States                        |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Worker Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Worker Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Default Account Worker Role" visible to a non permissioned user
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

